<h1>Software Research & Development Agreement</h1>

<p>This Agreement is entered into as of ___, 2026, by and between <strong>LAiSON.ORG</strong> and the <strong>Massachusetts State Police</strong>.</p>

<div class="section">
<h2>1. Purpose</h2>
<p>To design and evaluate software systems to assist in identifying indicators of human trafficking and related criminal activity in compliance with applicable law.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>2. Consideration</h2>
<p>The parties agree to the sum of <strong>$1.00</strong> as sufficient consideration.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>3. Scope of Work</h2>
<p>Developer shall create a proof-of-concept system including data correlation, pattern detection, analytical dashboards, and compliance controls using lawful data sources.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>4. Compliance</h2>
<p>The System shall align with federal law including the Paperwork Reduction Act, USA PATRIOT Act, and CJIS Security Policy, and shall respect constitutional protections.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>5. Data Restrictions</h2>
<p>Only lawfully obtained or publicly available data may be used. No unauthorized system access is permitted.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>6. Ethical Safeguards</h2>
<p>Outputs are investigative leads only and require human review. No mass surveillance or discriminatory profiling is permitted.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>7. Intellectual Property</h2>
<p>Developer retains ownership of all underlying systems. Agency receives a limited internal-use license.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>8. Liability</h2>
<p>Developer is not responsible for operational use or investigative outcomes.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>9. Term</h2>
<p>This Agreement remains in effect for ___ months unless terminated.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>10. Confidentiality</h2>
<p>Both parties agree to protect sensitive and proprietary information.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>11. Independent Contractor</h2>
<p>Developer operates as an independent contractor.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>12. Governing Law</h2>
<p>This Agreement is governed by Massachusetts law and applicable federal law.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>13. Entire Agreement</h2>
<p>This document constitutes the entire agreement between the parties and supersedes all prior discussions.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>14. Future Engagement & Commercialization</h2>
<p>In the event the Agency determines that the System, or any portion thereof, demonstrates operational value, the Agency agrees to enter into good faith negotiations with Developer for a subsequent production, deployment, and maintenance agreement.</p>

<p>Developer shall have a <strong>Right of First Negotiation (ROFN)</strong> for a period of twelve (12) months following completion of the prototype phase.</p>

<p>No third-party engagement for substantially similar systems shall occur during this period without first providing Developer the opportunity to submit a proposal.</p>
</div>

